// Folding and sweeping, in that order and twice: a fold turns a comparison
// into the value it was testing, which leaves the comparison dead, and the
// sweep that removes it can expose another fold. Two rounds reach a fixed
// point on everything the current folds can do; a third changes nothing, which
// is why the loop is written out rather than iterated.
opt_clean(int f) {
  op_fold(f);
  op_dce(f);
  opt_clean2(f);
} return void;

opt_clean2(int f) {
  op_fold(f);
  op_dce(f);
} return void;
